      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "A 402 error indicates that your Stripe API request is subject to an hourly quota limit and you haven't reached the maximum yet. To troubleshoot this, first check if you've already hit a rate limit for API calls with Stripe, then make sure your request payload is correctly formatted, all parameters are included for the requested action, and keys are valid. Check your Stripe API key (publishable key) and endpoint URL. For example, you might need something like `https://api.stripe.com/v1/checkout/sessions` for creating a checkout session. Double-check the parameters required for `checkout/sessions`, such as `payment_method_types` and `line_items`. Review the Stripe API documentation to ensure you're sending the right payload structure.",
